From 2038837d1dcb087777912295444f694f96b4e925 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:15:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B13b: find siblings of short no-year titles by the identity
 term

B13's 1,000-candidate window misses the versions of a short, common
title with no year ("Up", "Heat"): the title phrase matches too many
longer titles. Siblings now require the v7 title_identity term (score
0, so ranking is unchanged) when the index has it Ready, and fall back
to the window on a Missing or Backfilling field. The identity rule
moves into the search crate as TitleIdentityParts, so the term and the
shown identity come from one definition.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
